---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NewsletterForm from '../components/NewsletterForm.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const schema = {
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About MatchTales',
  description: 'MatchTales exists to tell you why the match, the round or the race matters.',
  url: `${SITE.url}/about`,
  isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
  mainEntity: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
};
---
<BaseLayout title="About MatchTales | Our Mission" description="MatchTales exists to democratise the story: the context, the rivalries and the reasons a match, a round or a race matters." keywords="about MatchTales, Why Care score, sports storytelling" schema={schema} imageAlt="About MatchTales">
  <main class="max-w-container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <header class="mt-10">
        <span class="text-[11px] font-sans font-medium text-pitch uppercase tracking-wide">Our mission</span>
        <h1 class="mt-2 font-head text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-tight">Everyone deserves to know why the match matters.</h1>
      </header>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[18px] leading-8">
        <p>Most sports apps will tell you the score. Lineups, possession, heat maps. What they will not tell you is the only thing that actually makes you care: <em>the story.</em></p>
        <p>MatchTales started as the story layer on the 2026 FIFA World Cup. Spain lifted the trophy on 19 July. The desk did not close. We now cover tennis, football, Formula 1, soccer, golf and basketball with the same question: why should you care about this one? Each sport has its own <a href="/sports" class="text-sky hover:underline">directory</a>.</p>
        <p>We give events a Why-Care score, then we tell you the human stake behind the number. A promoted side beating Manchester United. A 21-year-old wasting five championship points and still winning Wimbledon. A Super Bowl rematch that opens the NFL year. A kid from Italy winning Monza from nineteenth.</p>
        <p>We write like humans, for humans. No jargon walls. If a scorer, a minute or a ranking is on the page, it is locked to a named source. If we cannot source it, we leave it off.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 rounded-card border border-border/80 bg-surface2/60 p-6">
        <h2 class="font-head text-lg font-semibold">A quick, honest note</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] font-sans text-muted leading-7">MatchTales is an independent fan project. We are not affiliated with FIFA, the NFL, NBA, WNBA, ATP, WTA, PGA Tour or Formula 1. Names and fixtures are referenced for editorial purposes. If two sources disagree, we print the score both agree on and we skip the rest.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-head text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Join the story</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted font-sans mb-4">One email, every matchday, telling you exactly what to care about.</p>
        <NewsletterForm />
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
